WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.540
- Welcome to The Tell Show.

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:05.341
We've got a wonderful,
hilarious guest this week.

00:00:05.341 --> 00:00:06.756
We're really excited.

00:00:06.756 --> 00:00:09.007
Lamorne Morris, he's
an actor and comedian.

00:00:09.007 --> 00:00:11.737
He plays Winston Bishop on New Girl,

00:00:11.737 --> 00:00:15.125
and he's also in Barbershop: The Next Cut,

00:00:15.125 --> 00:00:16.405
which is out this week.

00:00:16.405 --> 00:00:19.893
(rhythmic peaceful music)

00:00:19.893 --> 00:00:22.631
So here on The Tell Show, Lamorne,

00:00:22.631 --> 00:00:25.180
we always try to open up with
a game of Never Have I Ever.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.804
- Each of us will say something
that we've never done,

00:00:27.804 --> 00:00:29.777
and then if you have done it,

00:00:29.777 --> 00:00:31.706
like if I'm like, "I've
never killed someone,"

00:00:31.706 --> 00:00:32.722
and Isaac's like, "Of course I have."

00:00:32.722 --> 00:00:34.542
- [Isaac] Whoa.
- You will ring a bell.

00:00:34.542 --> 00:00:35.496
(dings)

00:00:35.496 --> 00:00:36.838
And then you'll talk about it.

00:00:36.838 --> 00:00:38.835
- I'm gonna start with never have I ever

00:00:38.835 --> 00:00:40.413
auditioned for a television show.

00:00:40.413 --> 00:00:41.949
(dings)

00:00:41.949 --> 00:00:44.456
- I auditioned 15 times for New Girl.

00:00:44.456 --> 00:00:45.309
- Wait, what?

00:00:45.309 --> 00:00:46.230
- It was crazy.
- [Summer Anne] Wow.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.598
- I auditioned for the
role of Coach originally,

00:00:48.598 --> 00:00:50.507
got offered the part, couldn't do it

00:00:50.507 --> 00:00:53.355
because the same day,
CBS offered me a role.

00:00:53.355 --> 00:00:55.382
The New Girl, when I turned down the role,

00:00:55.382 --> 00:00:57.522
they ended up offering it
to Damon Wayans Junior.

00:00:57.522 --> 00:01:00.111
They weren't anticipating
that his show, Happy Endings,

00:01:00.111 --> 00:01:01.970
was getting picked up for a second season.

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:03.108
- Damn.

00:01:03.108 --> 00:01:04.868
This is like street fight stuff.

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:06.030
(laughs)

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:07.748
- Yeah, and so because he left,

00:01:07.748 --> 00:01:09.955
that left a space open
for another character,

00:01:09.955 --> 00:01:12.024
and so they came up with
the character, Winston,

00:01:12.024 --> 00:01:15.992
and in doing so, they had
to audition 11 more times.

00:01:15.992 --> 00:01:19.217
- So you auditioned a normal
amount of times the first time,

00:01:19.217 --> 00:01:20.742
got the part.
- [Lamorne] Yes.

00:01:20.742 --> 00:01:22.977
- And then because of all that kerfuffle,

00:01:22.977 --> 00:01:25.609
you then had to come in, and
then that was 11 more times.

00:01:25.609 --> 00:01:28.670
- Yes it was a nightmare
indeed, but it was fun,

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:31.542
'cause like, we built up
chemistry with the cast already.

00:01:31.542 --> 00:01:34.176
It was literally a first-name
basis when you walk in.

00:01:34.176 --> 00:01:35.142
"Lamorne, what's up?"

00:01:35.142 --> 00:01:35.975
"Oh hey, Jake."

00:01:35.975 --> 00:01:36.808
"Hey Zooey, what's goin' on?"

00:01:36.808 --> 00:01:37.641
(laughs)

00:01:37.641 --> 00:01:39.083
And I knew that they liked me

00:01:39.083 --> 00:01:41.800
because they treated me differently.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:43.044
Actor would come out the room,

00:01:43.044 --> 00:01:44.559
and Zooey would walk by and go,

00:01:44.559 --> 00:01:45.700
"Nah, that wasn't the guy."

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:46.533
(laughs)

00:01:46.533 --> 00:01:47.740
And I would go, "Yes!"

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.276
She's directing this to me.

00:01:49.276 --> 00:01:50.942
- What do you got Summer Anne?

00:01:50.942 --> 00:01:52.206
- Never have I ever stood someone up.

00:01:52.206 --> 00:01:53.266
(dings)

00:01:53.266 --> 00:01:54.801
(disgusted groans)

00:01:54.801 --> 00:01:56.219
- Okay here's the story.

00:01:56.219 --> 00:01:58.193
I was living in San Francisco at the time

00:01:58.193 --> 00:02:00.614
in a one bedroom with
like four other people,

00:02:00.614 --> 00:02:02.374
and like pigeons in the walls,

00:02:02.374 --> 00:02:04.134
and like mice that I'm like friends with,

00:02:04.134 --> 00:02:05.350
and like eating cereal.

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.665
Basically I had worked my butt off

00:02:07.665 --> 00:02:09.478
to get this job at this bar,

00:02:09.478 --> 00:02:10.939
and at that time, an old friend

00:02:10.939 --> 00:02:12.262
of mine from college had moved down,

00:02:12.262 --> 00:02:14.640
and he started working at
this company called Facebook.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:15.504
- Oh!

00:02:15.504 --> 00:02:16.845
- And so my buddy, his name's Mike,

00:02:16.845 --> 00:02:18.445
my buddy, Mike, kinda calls me up.

00:02:18.445 --> 00:02:20.589
He's like, "Look, we're
really staffing up right now.

00:02:20.589 --> 00:02:21.954
"We're really growing."

00:02:21.954 --> 00:02:24.183
And I was like, "That's
like for college kids."

00:02:24.183 --> 00:02:26.829
And my reply to Mike was, "You
know, I really worked hard

00:02:26.829 --> 00:02:28.802
"to get this job at this bar.

00:02:28.802 --> 00:02:31.215
"I kinda feel like (laughs)

00:02:31.215 --> 00:02:34.036
"I kinda feel like things are starting

00:02:34.036 --> 00:02:35.520
"to turn around for me.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:36.965
"I feel like Facebook, you never know

00:02:36.965 --> 00:02:37.798
"if that's going anywhere.

00:02:37.798 --> 00:02:40.129
"That's for kids, that's college stuff.

00:02:40.129 --> 00:02:41.686
"And I really appreciate the opportunity."

00:02:41.686 --> 00:02:43.169
He's like, "Look, here's the
meeting, here's the time,

00:02:43.169 --> 00:02:44.982
"just come."

00:02:44.982 --> 00:02:46.465
- And you didn't go.
- [Isaac] And I didn't go.

00:02:46.465 --> 00:02:48.694
It should note that Mike now owns a house

00:02:48.694 --> 00:02:50.625
on top of Bernal Hill in San Francisco.

00:02:50.625 --> 00:02:52.737
I was one of his groomsmen.

00:02:52.737 --> 00:02:55.681
He flew me out and bought me
a $1,000 suit for his wedding.

00:02:55.681 --> 00:02:57.238
He's looking at another house.

00:02:57.238 --> 00:02:59.094
(disgusted groans)

00:02:59.094 --> 00:03:00.545
- You stood up Mark Zuckerberg.

00:03:00.545 --> 00:03:01.378
(laughing)

00:03:01.378 --> 00:03:02.731
- Mark was waiting with a clipboard going,

00:03:02.731 --> 00:03:03.990
"Oh, I love this guy so much.

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:06.027
"I just wanna, oh, check the
right boxes for this guy."

00:03:06.027 --> 00:03:08.032
- "Yeah, I just wanna give
him like lots of options."

00:03:08.032 --> 00:03:09.656
- "Oh, he's gonna be the one."

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:10.813
(laughing)

00:03:10.813 --> 00:03:12.768
- My like good way of looking at my way

00:03:12.768 --> 00:03:14.208
that I can still get out
of bed every morning,

00:03:14.208 --> 00:03:17.151
knowing that I just like took that wrong

00:03:17.151 --> 00:03:18.386
of a choice in my life,

00:03:18.386 --> 00:03:20.498
is I was just like, with
that much money, I'd be dead.

00:03:20.498 --> 00:03:22.514
Like there would've been a boat accident.

00:03:22.514 --> 00:03:24.327
(laughing)

00:03:24.327 --> 00:03:25.767
- So we continuing the game?

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:28.543
- Yeah, now you got your never,
something you've never done.

00:03:28.543 --> 00:03:30.126
- Never have I ever

00:03:31.384 --> 00:03:34.382
made out with a co-worker of mine.

00:03:34.382 --> 00:03:35.769
- What are you implying?

00:03:35.769 --> 00:03:39.559
- I'm implying I feel like if
y'all host this show together,

00:03:39.559 --> 00:03:42.129
that at some point, some
penetration is goin' on!

00:03:42.129 --> 00:03:43.548
(laughing)

00:03:43.548 --> 00:03:44.988
I don't know, I don't know.

00:03:44.988 --> 00:03:45.852
(dings)

00:03:45.852 --> 00:03:46.705
Oh!

00:03:46.705 --> 00:03:48.867
- Look, I have made out with a co-worker,

00:03:48.867 --> 00:03:50.862
but not at my current job.

00:03:50.862 --> 00:03:53.187
I worked at a bookstore
for like seven years

00:03:53.187 --> 00:03:55.736
in my early 20s, and 20 to 27,

00:03:55.736 --> 00:03:57.987
the only people I hooked
up with were my coworkers.

00:03:57.987 --> 00:03:59.896
(laughing)

00:03:59.896 --> 00:04:01.400
- Dirty.
(laughing)

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.606
- That's nasty.

00:04:02.606 --> 00:04:04.376
- I mean, there was a lot of sex

00:04:04.376 --> 00:04:05.646
that happened at the bookstore.

00:04:05.646 --> 00:04:06.479
- Lot of sticky pages.

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:07.312
- That's true.

00:04:07.312 --> 00:04:08.770
That is true, holiday parties were--

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:10.120
- Did you ever sleep with your boss?

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:11.332
- I slept with my boss, yeah.

00:04:11.332 --> 00:04:13.944
(laughing)

00:04:13.944 --> 00:04:16.717
- [Isaac] So casual about it.
- That's awesome.

00:04:16.717 --> 00:04:18.477
I wanna be that boss, though, that's like,

00:04:18.477 --> 00:04:19.992
"Yeah, I fucked all my employees."

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:21.101
"Where do you work, a porn shop?"

00:04:21.101 --> 00:04:21.942
"No, a book store."

00:04:21.942 --> 00:04:23.000
(laughing)

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.493
- Yeah, I mean there was like,

00:04:24.493 --> 00:04:27.907
there was a web of like sexual misconduct

00:04:27.907 --> 00:04:29.389
happening at that bookstore.

00:04:29.389 --> 00:04:31.320
Book People, Austin, Texas.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:32.504
- Wow, you just shout 'em out!

00:04:32.504 --> 00:04:34.147
(laughing)

00:04:34.147 --> 00:04:36.402
- Great place, I wanna be
clear, great place to buy.

00:04:36.402 --> 00:04:37.653
- Great bookstore, great bookstore.

00:04:37.653 --> 00:04:38.737
- Yeah, great place to buy books.

00:04:38.737 --> 00:04:41.027
- So if I went into Book
People in Austin, Texas,

00:04:41.027 --> 00:04:43.629
I might be standing in the wet spot.

00:04:43.629 --> 00:04:44.877
(laughing)

00:04:44.877 --> 00:04:45.805
That could be--

00:04:45.805 --> 00:04:47.299
- I mean, it's been years, but you know.

00:04:47.299 --> 00:04:48.525
- I'm gonna go in there with a black light

00:04:48.525 --> 00:04:49.438
and see what I can find.

00:04:49.438 --> 00:04:51.576
(laughing)

00:04:51.576 --> 00:04:54.125
(upbeat music)

00:04:54.125 --> 00:04:56.077
- [Isaac] Poor Book People. (laughing)

00:04:56.077 --> 00:04:57.635
I think that could be
great for their business

00:04:57.635 --> 00:04:59.142
